/// Layer 3 — cascade layers.
///
/// Declared in one place, in priority order, before anything writes into them.
/// A `@layer` statement that appears after a rule that uses the layer creates
/// the layer at *that* point in the cascade instead, which is how a stylesheet
/// ends up with correct-looking rules that lose to the wrong neighbour.
///
/// The order below is the whole contract:
///
/// - `reset`      — normalisation. Loses to everything.
/// - `tokens`     — custom property declarations.
/// - `base`       — bare element styling.
/// - `components` — the design system.
/// - `utilities`  — single-purpose overrides. Beats components by design.
///
/// Anything unlayered beats all of these, which is the escape hatch for
/// third-party CSS you cannot move.
@layer reset, tokens, base, components, utilities;
